From b65c59d853eca608f3de61c9d839b793fff040f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 17:03:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] configstore: extend tenant_id to teams, VKs, budgets, rate
 limits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 1 schema rollout step 2. Adds tenant_id (default "default") to
the four remaining core governance entities:
  - governance_teams
  - governance_virtual_keys
  - governance_budgets
  - governance_rate_limits

One unified migration (add_tenant_id_to_governance_tables) iterates
the four target tables, AddColumn + idempotent backfill via UPDATE
... WHERE tenant_id IS NULL OR tenant_id = '' (Postgres respects the
column default but older SQLite may not honor it on existing rows).

Provider configs, MCP configs, and other child entities are
intentionally NOT touched here — they belong to a tenant transitively
via the owning VK or team. A future migration can promote tenant_id
to those rows if a row-level scoping pass shows the joins are too
expensive.

Backward-compatible by construction: single-tenant deployments keep
working, every existing governance row ends up assigned to the
DefaultTenantID seeded by the previous migration.

Test: TestMigrationAddTenantIDToGovernanceTables_AppliesToAllFour
asserts the column landed on all four tables, the column default
kicks in for new inserts that omit TenantID, and the migration is
idempotent on re-run.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
